{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789848238,"nonce":"3VH2NxbJmFRHdKj99C3uy8gakCE=","title":"An if-expression as a list literal's item stores nil","message":"In a typed-AST function built with the builtins DSL (zyntax_builtins::build), a list literal whose item is an if_expr (TypedExpression::If used as a value), for example\n\n    list(vec![if_expr(cond, box_bool(bool(true)), nil()), box_str(if_expr(c2, text(\"a\"), text(\"b\"))), box_i64(n)], anys)\n\ncomes out with every item nil at run time under Cranelift, with no diagnostic. Seen in the Lua library's zl_os_execute (crates/zyntax_lua/src/library/stdlib.rs, os_declarations) where the tuple returned by os.execute printed nil nil nil; binding each item to a local first gives the right values. Earlier the same shape crashed Cranelift (store: no value); the Lua frontend hoists list items for that reason (Lowerer::array_of). The library DSL has no such hoist, so the lowering of a list literal with a conditional item is the place to fix: an If in value position inside an aggregate literal is lowered into a block that the literal's stores do not follow.","files":null}]}